title: Seeckt's Decree
subtitle: The general with emergency powers turns on the extremes.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month >= 11 and crisis = 0 and e23_ban_done = 0 and beer_hall_putsch = 1
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_ban_done = 1;
var ban = (Q.german_october >= 1 || Q.e23_october_path > 0 || Q.militancy >= 50) ? 1 : 0;
Q.kpd_banned = ban;
if (ban) {
    Q.repression += 15;
    for (var d of Q.districts) {
        Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.9;
    }
} else {
    Q.repression += 4;
}
Q.nsdap_exists = 1;
Q.sa_strength *= 0.6;
!}

= Seeckt's Decree

After the putsch in Munich, President Ebert transfers executive power in the whole Reich to General Hans von Seeckt himself. Seeckt has no wish to be a dictator, he says, only to restore order. On 23 November he bans Hitler's National Socialists and the German Völkisch Freedom Party.

[? if kpd_banned = 1 : He bans the Communist Party of Germany in the same decree. Its offices are closed, its presses sealed, *Die Rote Fahne* forbidden. Its deputies keep their immunity, and nothing else. Thousands of functionaries are arrested in the first week. ?]

[? if kpd_banned = 0 : He does not ban us. The party took no part in any rising, the SPD has let it be known that it would leave the government over a ban, and Stresemann has no wish to make martyrs. The police keep their lists up to date all the same. ?]

- @underground: Build the illegal apparatus: cells, couriers, hidden presses.
- @legal: Fight it in the courts and the Reichstag, with whoever will help.
- @defy: Defy it openly: our papers appear anyway.
- @use: Use our legality: recruit the workers the others have lost.

@underground
subtitle: The party survives as a conspiracy, disciplined and small.
view-if: kpd_banned = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.unity += 5;
Q.red_guards_loyalty += 5;
Q.worker_support -= 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

The party splits into cells of five. Leaflets are printed in cellars and handed out at dawn. The membership falls, and those who stay can be trusted.

@legal
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The SPD's left wing and the civil-liberties lawyers help. Slow.
view-if: kpd_banned = 1
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids asking the social democrats for help.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.spd_relation += 5;
Q.repression -= 5;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

[? if levi_split = 1 : Paul Levi, from the SPD benches, is the first to denounce the ban in the Reichstag. ?] Our deputies and their lawyers fight the ban case by case. Some presses are unsealed by the courts within weeks.

@defy
subtitle: Brave, and the arrests double.
view-if: kpd_banned = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.repression += 8;
Q.militancy += 5;
Q.worker_support += 2;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.95;
}
!}

*Die Rote Fahne* appears under a new name every week, and every week the police seize it.

@use
subtitle: Recruits the disappointed, from the left and the right.
view-if: kpd_banned = 0
on-arrival: {!
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.05;
}
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 3;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 3;
!}

With the National Socialists banned and the SPD in disgrace with its own members, our meetings are full all through December.
